{
  "generator": "tools/kits/buildings.py (procedural bpy kit, no paid generation)",
  "conventions": {
    "units": "metres, Y up (Godot), origin = footprint centre on the ground, door/front faces -Z",
    "footprint": "faction-doc cells x 0.5 m (kingdom.md 7.2, clans.md 7; art bible 1.3, decided 2026-10-19): supply 8x8 (4 m, 3-3.5 m tall), production / altar / shop / research 12x12 (6 m, 5-6 m; altar and shops 4.5-5.5 m), towers 4x4 (2 m, 6-8 m), halls 16x16 (8 m). Ground geometry stays inside the footprint (outside_footprint_m reports the overshoot below / above 1.5 m: eaves, pennants and streamers may reach ~0.3 m out)",
    "ground": "every building stands on an irregular ground apron covering its footprint: top 1.5 cm above y = 0 (packed earth with a timber kerb and cobbles for the kingdom, trampled earth with a drystone curb and felt rugs for the clans), a skirt down to -0.2 m so terrain bumps never open a gap",
    "facing": "door on -Z like units; UnitView draws structures at a fixed world yaw of PI so the door always faces the RTS camera (which sits on +Z) whatever the sim facing",
    "materials": "<id> = opaque faction atlas (textures/<faction>_buildings_atlas.jpg, tileable swatches at 144 px/m, pattern periods matched to the AI halls: roof courses ~0.3 m, rubble stones 0.4-0.7 m); <id>_GLOW = windows / embers / smoke-ring glow (textures/buildings_glow.png; shipped with emissiveFactor 0 for day, extras emissive_night = the dusk value to set at 17:45, bible 1.5); <id>_TEAM = light grey cloth (textures/buildings_team.png), UnitView multiplies albedo_color by the player colour. Primitive order GLOW, atlas, TEAM (Godot 4.7's glTF import skips vertex_color_use_as_albedo on a mesh's first primitive; buildings without GLOW start with a hidden 1 mm dummy triangle)",
    "COLOR_0": "RGB = painted AO (ray-cast crevices, ground contact) x top light x per-part tint; A = 1",
    "TEXCOORD_1": "x = build layer (0 frame / lattice / walls, 1 covering: roofs, felt), y = normalized height (0 ground .. 1 top)"
  },
  "build_progress": {
    "approach": "no _construction meshes: tools/kits/build_reveal.gdshader reveals the finished mesh bottom-up. Height = object-space VERTEX.y / model_height (set it to height_m; AI halls: their AABB height), so it needs no vertex data and works on the AI halls and hall upgrades too",
    "kingdom": "scaffold-raised: two_pass = false; a ragged hash-noise edge with an ember glow; scaffold and ladders are particles / a separate shared prop",
    "clans": "Raising, two_pass = true: UV2.x = 0 (lattice, masts, stone ring) rises over progress 0..0.6, UV2.x = 1 (felt walls and domes, team bands) over 0.4..1.0",
    "uniforms": "albedo_tex, albedo_color (team colour on TEAM surfaces), use_vertex_color, emission_tex, emission, progress, model_height, two_pass, band, edge_color, edge_energy"
  },
  "team_coverage": "team_coverage_rts = visible TEAM fraction of the silhouette from the 56 deg RTS pitch, front view and mean of 4 yaws (art bible 3.1 asks 6-10 % for buildings, the kit brief 12-18 %: the kit aims at ~8-15 %, at least one team area in the upper third)",
